      ["Remove the bottom rack and clean the filter under running water, along with the sump area; do it monthly.", "Check the spray arms spin freely and clear their holes with a toothpick.", "Run the garbage disposal if the dishwasher drains into it; on a new installation, check the knockout plug was removed from the disposal inlet.",
       "Check the drain hose for kinks and make sure it has a high loop under the counter (or an air gap) so waste water cannot flow back.", "Run a cycle with a cup of white vinegar on the top rack, or a dishwasher cleaner, to dissolve limescale and grease.", "A leak at the door usually means a dirty or worn gasket: wipe it, and replace it if it is cracked.",
       "Use a rinse aid, load so water can reach every dish, and run the hot tap until it is hot before starting."],
      ["Toothpicks", "Towels", "White vinegar", "Pliers", "Flashlight"], _MAINS + "Turn off the water supply before disconnecting hoses.",
